<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Deadly Russian attacks damage two bridges in Kyiv, mayor says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5a1120bee16d06d70400d01e4f791959a8b61e86e0febb7716e94fc321eeff0</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T06:32:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says--388c1dca5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says" /><summary type="html">Russian attacks on Kyiv killed three people and damaged two bridges in the Ukrainian capital, city authorities said on Friday. The fresh wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" retaliation after Ukraine this week damaged the Crimea bridge. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Czechs protest en masse against 'concentration of power in one hand' and growing control over media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d21b47fa8032fedb2474cb516ce31cc3762608cd6dbcea9a2e92cd580c57a57</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T06:02:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over--9a7dcdecced1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media" /><summary type="html">As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Mikuláš Minář, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement, joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK set to sign deals on trade, energy, youth mobility at Brussels summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b03d58a12df5ec09b7a9e362452cfcf1f399cca6d4f068a966c4eb625a1b77a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T02:00:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit--38d65333a954.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit" /><summary type="html">The UK and the EU are poised to agree new deals on trade, energy and youth mobility at a summit in Brussels on Friday, as part of UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's bid to reset ties with the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>PM Sanchez admits 'mistakes' in key debate ahead of Spain's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a87a6debefe6f38e1d061053e8ce829a476a8fab1b7e6127cc77c0f4367dbee</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T00:49:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s_nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election--31911ebf68da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s%C3%A1nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez acknowledged shortcomings in his government on Thursday as he faced conservative rival Alberto Nunez Feijoo in the campaign's only televised debate. The November 29 election could leave the far-right Vox party in a position to enter government.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes on Kyiv kill one, damage Dutch and Austrian embassies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd831dac198fb91edf141da4a11fb1c14ee3dbb1e5babd816827974d4eda502c</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T21:25:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies--b11b79f67545.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies" /><summary type="html">A wave of daytime Russian strikes on Kyiv on Thursday killed one person and damaged a historic cathedral as well as the embassies of Austria and the Netherlands. Loud explosions erupted across the Ukraine capital throughout the day as the leaders of Russia, China and the United States held a historic meeting in China that put Russia's President Vladimir Putin in international spotlight. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kushner says Trump 'open' to extend NATO mutual defense-type clause to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:705069c065fbc85ccda774fee487a00aae0d9ab586f995a07bd6764487e0c6a4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine--5d7323eefe85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine" /><summary type="html">US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday that President Donald Trump was open to extending to Ukraine a security guarantee similar to NATO's mutual defense clause, but stressed that Washington has to protect its interests too. The comments came as German Chancellor Friedrich Merz qualified the summit between the presidents of the United States, Russia and China as a "photo op". FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator Douglas Herbert explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron urges Ukraine's allies to 'reopen the question' of NATO membership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9672f7756f82faed7bfafa1125ba1bb3d267a0049a5122155eafccace31bc398</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:32:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership--3461324b88d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called for Ukraine's allies to speed up the delivery of urgently needed air defence systems and urged them to "reopen the question" of Ukraine's NATO membership after talks in Berlin aimed at reaffirming European support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Three of a kind? Xi hosts Trump and Putin as Ukraine war grinds on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e0f4c592b8c8c03c43c6c96fb4e7454c46afaefbe5ca5c3ebd8b2108b82b5b7</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:39:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on--0d31e6ae5346.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on" /><summary type="html">Gang of three or glorified photo op? Xi Jinping hosting Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Already, our Monday panel rejected attempts to paint the three-way meeting as a new Yalta, as in the 1945 sit-down on the Black Sea that defined the post-war security architecture of Europe.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea094185d2392ecc05093db21207e68dc209ac868dcf9c48b7ff5a416a790b53</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications--7c816cd4e664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications" /><summary type="html">The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?</summary></entry><entry><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bcbafc4026d7aa3585d103ee0a9c18e572c4457ff05509535383ba5d1c96c02</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin--41fb764541d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:846c3edceaed67999ba3d790c8fface0990f79e485f995e42504dc708afc7b5e</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support--2eee6bb2adfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6a8a63d1d63c33b4a51fdc3f015c6db168babd362398fa37914f98fbd6c0616</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:08:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump--274d8e9dcbf1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump" /><summary type="html">Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin to rally support for Kyiv after Trump-Putin-Xi talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95175e0ed9ad34ceed00901547ebfb62f5ddea8c16c607fde98c55abd58b86e4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:55:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks--3d07d30f658f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin on Thursday to shore up support for Kyiv just hours after Russia's Vladimir Putin took part in a historic trilateral meeting with US President Donald Trump and China's Xi Jinping. The "Coalition of the Willing" summit comes as Europe is hoping to secure a seat at the table of any future peace talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:724b81326c02dddfed36006cd14395beb6fb59dfe722e938d91a53300e96e91f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding--3de44bf4c890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding" /><summary type="html">Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33d3bd5035d05cb413a77b7a30bbc070e921a813d4308edc3af85c6b2daad053</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T21:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack--caeee115f4a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10d5b66693261565a5cd8d6a5365711a82f17ae2899bce7c968d8ed05e9ddaf9</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea--968a1a06351e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6250f1eb01b9535d35d2fa530f2fcb5f018e6d84bbff6ca100ef18bad76f914a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:57:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia--95e35187e67d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia" /><summary type="html">An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia’s new low-cost munitions pose a fresh threat to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7bdcf2b19170b126b2fc9bfbb0128a58f67ca8bd43a45050fcb4d46158a106c</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine--81011c427b6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Dan-T, Filin and Geran-5 might not mean anything to you, but in Ukraine, everyone is talking about these munitions. These new Russian weapons are small, fast and cheap – and a major threat, as they were specially designed to get around Ukrainian anti-aircraft defences and strike deep within the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes new €45 billion Ukraine loan to be repaid by Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e8ddb77f5fc1fdfc486bbfc5cd540eca45894654d72529fb735fd97e59ced46</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-eu-proposes-new-_45-billion-ukraine-loan-to-be-repaid-by-russia--b080f0b0d8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-eu-proposes-new-%E2%82%AC45-billion-ukraine-loan-to-be-repaid-by-russia" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von ⁠der Leyen announced on Wednesday a proposed €45 billion loan to Ukraine for 2027 to help cover around two-thirds ​of Kyiv's financing ​needs. The loan will be repaid ⁠through future ⁠war reparations by Russia, von der Leyen added.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy approves anti-semitism law despite concerns over freedom of expression</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27dcf091534518df90294a5e7fb3b62551e2d13acfa99edfa11de2fa40e6b78f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T07:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-italy-approves-anti-semitism-law-despite-concerns-over-freedom-of-expression--ddabda07c6bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-italy-approves-anti-semitism-law-despite-concerns-over-freedom-of-expression" /><summary type="html">Italy's ​parliament on Tuesday approved a new bill aimed at combating anti-semitism – which lists some forms of criticism of ⁠Israel as examples of anti-semitic conduct – despite concerns that it could limit freedom of expression and advocacy for Palestinian rights. The law will not impose financial ⁠penalties or criminal sanctions for offenders.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Authorities take over Turkey's last pro-opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01c0f75cc1644d8436d030398138166070efbdd7290754c677ab226577005b90</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T19:58:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/authorities-take-over-turkey-s-last-pro-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv--b9a43ba1ff5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/authorities-take-over-turkey-s-last-pro-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv" /><summary type="html">Police raided the Istanbul headquarters of Sozcu TV on Tuesday, dealing another significant blow to Turkey's pro-opposition media. This is the third such seizure of pro-opposition media in just over a year. It comes amid public uproar over a multi-billion investment fund scandal that has affected the savings of nearly half a million people and piled pressure on President Recep Tayyip Erdogan's ruling AKP party ahead of elections in 2028. FRANCE 24's Jasper Mortimer reports from Ankara.</summary></entry><entry><title>Estonia closes its border with Russia but can it keep Moscow out?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4f473efbffd903ff6632c442b4b3a6a2405c36458af85e3ac3308d86723114c</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:28:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-estonia-closes-its-border-with-russia-but-can-it-keep-moscow-out--8ad536e1b952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-estonia-closes-its-border-with-russia-but-can-it-keep-moscow-out" /><summary type="html">Estonia announced this weekend it would close its border with Russia, after blaming its eastern neighbour of attempting to sabotage one of its drone factories. But at a time when the internet has become one of Russia’s most potent weapons to wage hybrid warfare, does closing the border even matter?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Two bridges in Kyiv heavily damaged by Russian strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee64e607ce65f4a92b3b7000b1f9aedcfe4a1d14f7adabfbf93520546f8b758</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:54:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261117-ukraine-two-bridges-in-kyiv-heavily-damaged-by-russian-strikes--7ea1ef9e1575.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261117-ukraine-two-bridges-in-kyiv-heavily-damaged-by-russian-strikes" /><summary type="html">Russia hit two major bridges in Kyiv while Ukraine struck Moscow's link to annexed Crimea for the second night in a row, officials said Tuesday, ahead of a historic meeting of Chinese, US and Russian leaders. Detals from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Data leak exposes Deutsche Bank ties to Russian oligarchs, Epstein and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a276c0ec40fb724bf386f7c60ddc753c0df1d840e60259c3790895806199c5b1</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T09:45:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261117-deutsche-bank-shares-drop-after-reports-on-mass-data-leak--3c18ba74004c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261117-deutsche-bank-shares-drop-after-reports-on-mass-data-leak" /><summary type="html">Shares in Deutsche Bank plunged Tuesday after international media outlets published reports detailing the bank's questionable business practices over the past 20 years, including its ties to Russian oligarchs, convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and Donald Trump before he became the US president.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine critically damages bridge linking occupied Crimea with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4b648ee99011a83eda51ffc5df9a9f8836bb84e7e4266b7b172d199d538b926</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T06:43:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-ukraine-critically-damages-bridge-linking-occupied-crimea-with-russia--6db84b4abe2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-ukraine-critically-damages-bridge-linking-occupied-crimea-with-russia" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian drones and missiles struck a vital bridge linking Russia to the occupied Crimean Peninsula, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Tuesday, calling it an “unprecedented” operation as Russia reported that its forces downed a record number of Ukrainian drones for the second straight day.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin arrives in China ahead of trilateral Trump-Xi summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e6fa1b62e786ba7c9d5d8a03e8226f00f4ea92c26ce7c198026551ae48dedb</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T01:38:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine--ed14a50b56b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday arrived in China where he is expected to meet with his US and Chinese counterparts Donald Trump and Xi Jinping on the sidelines of the APEC summit, Russian state media reported. Russian state news agency TASS said that Putin's plane has landed at Shenzhen's Bao'an International Airport. Putin will take part in the summit later this week. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes hit two key bridges in Kyiv, disrupting water and power supplies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:985ebb6075eec7851a9a48da4927a94e9892d3c57a627c7b2fed34ad99752c2d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T00:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine--88719774137a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian forces struck two major bridges crossing the Dnipro River in Kyiv late Monday, damaging critical infrastructure and causing water and power cuts in parts of the Ukrainian capital, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said. The attacks came as Moscow launched a wider wave of drone and missile strikes across Ukraine, including in the regions of Cherkasy and Kharkiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555e577b43786f8689cc3fa8033b7615924d45e6c8b19f65a67c0df7569bb5e0</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:07:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--d261bbeac259.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, a journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d89013418bf1ee4a9300af0059be137e92147859ae6a960fbfc686f1a005999</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:05:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--784c998c6cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, a journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hard bargain: Should Ukraine trade Donbas for NATO membership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbd5ad8c81acaea0918544bcb23a5f95482bc76d283acf9faed8f95d93d22c03</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:27:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership--a0b9c11071ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is asserting that the United States has asked him about a straight-up swap: Russia gets the Donbas and the rest of Ukraine gets NATO membership – a guarantee against Moscow later having a second go and annexing the entire country. Whether or not the offer is real, serious or either side would accept it is another matter. We ask if the talk of partition signals some kind of turning point in a nearly five-year war that's at a brutal stalemate.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry></feed>
